# FuelBorn — credentials inventory (template)

> This is the **template**. The real values live at:
>
> * `infra/CREDS.md` locally (gitignored)
> * `/root/pods-ml-creds.md` on the VM (mode 0640, root:podsadmin)
>
> Copy this file to `infra/CREDS.md`, fill in real values, and treat it as
> the single source of truth for "what's the password to X." Rotate after
> any compromise and update this file.

---

## Local workstation → server access

| Key | Value |
|---|---|
| SSH private key | `~/.ssh/<keyname>` (mode 0600 — never check in) |
| SSH public key fingerprint | `SHA256:<fingerprint>` |
| VM user | `podsadmin` |
| Connect command | `ssh podsadmin@<fqdn>` |

## Azure

| Key | Value |
|---|---|
| Subscription | `<name>` |
| Account | `<email>` |
| Tenant ID | `<GUID>` |
| Login command | `az login` |
| Resource group | `PODS-ML-PROTOTYPE` (eastus) |
| Node 1 VM | `pods-ml-prototype` — public `172.174.92.191` / vnet `10.0.0.4` |
| Node 2 VM | `pods-ml-node2` — public `20.51.150.92` / vnet `10.0.0.5` |
| Both NICs | `pods-ml-prototypeVNET` / `pods-ml-prototypeSubnet` (`10.0.0.0/24`) |
| NSG | `pods-ml-prototype-nsg` (shared by both NICs) |

## Tailscale (cross-node networking — see `infra/TAILSCALE.md`)

| Key | Value |
|---|---|
| Account email | `<email>` |
| Auth key (reusable, non-ephemeral) | `tskey-auth-…` |
| Node 1 tailnet name / IP | `pods-ml-node1` / `100.105.7.103` |
| Node 2 tailnet name / IP | `pods-ml-node2` / `100.92.124.106` |
| Admin (route approval) | <https://login.tailscale.com/admin/machines> |
| ACL editor | <https://login.tailscale.com/admin/acls/file> |
| Node 1 advertised subnet | `172.18.0.0/16` (docker bridge `pelican_nw`) |
| Node 2 advertised subnet | `172.21.0.0/16` (docker bridge `pelican_nw`) |

## DNS

| Zone | Records |
|---|---|
| `pods.ml` (Cloudflare, DNS only) | A `pods.ml` / `app.pods.ml` / `www.pods.ml` → `172.174.92.191` |
| `bigcat.pw` (Cloudflare, DNS only) | A `*` → `172.174.92.191` ; MX `inbox` → Resend |

