## Pelican Panel (Docker Compose)

| Key | Value |
|---|---|
| Panel container | `pelican-panel-1` |
| Panel UI | `https://<fqdn>/admin` |
| Admin user (email / username) | `<your-admin-email>` / `<admin-username>` |
| Admin password | `<set via php artisan p:user:make on first install>` |
| `APP_KEY` | `<32-char base64 — Laravel encryption key>` |
| `APP_URL` | `https://<fqdn>` |

## MariaDB (panel database)

| Key | Value |
|---|---|
| Container | `pelican-database-1` |
| Image | `mariadb:10.11` |
| Host (from panel) | `database` |
| Database | `panel` |
| `MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD` | `<48-char hex>` |
| `MYSQL_USER` | `pelican` |
| `MYSQL_PASSWORD` | `<48-char hex — same as DB_PASSWORD in panel env>` |

## Wings (host binary, not a container)

| Key | Value |
|---|---|
| Config | `/etc/pelican/config.yml` (root:wings 0640) |
| Node UUID | `<from panel: Admin → Nodes → ID>` |
| `token_id` | `<16-char id, paired with the panel node>` |
| `token` | `<64-char secret — DO NOT share>` |
| API port | `8080` (TLS via Let's Encrypt cert syncd by `/usr/local/sbin/sync-cert.sh`) |
| SFTP port | `2022` |
| Data volumes root | `/srv/pods/wings/volumes` |

## Caddy (TLS + reverse proxy)

| Key | Value |
|---|---|
| Config | `/etc/caddy/Caddyfile` |
| Cloudflare token (for `*.bigcat.pw` DNS-01) | `/etc/caddy/cloudflare.env` → `CF_API_TOKEN=cfut_...` |
| Access log | `/var/log/caddy/pods/access.log` (rotated 50MB × 4) |
| Per-pod includes | `/etc/caddy/domains/<slug>.caddy` (regenerable via `pods-ml-domain`) |
| Wildcard cert | Renewed by Caddy via Cloudflare token; staging fallback in same dir |

## Cloudflare

| Key | Value |
|---|---|
| Zone | `bigcat.pw` |
| Account email | `<the email on the CF account>` |
| API token name | `pods-ml-caddy-dns01` |
| API token value | `<cfut_… — DNS edit scoped to bigcat.pw>` |
| DNS proxy mode | **DNS only (gray cloud)** — required for the wildcard cert |

## FuelBorn frontend (Next.js)

| Key | Value |
|---|---|
| Service | `pods-ml-frontend.service` |
| Env file | `/srv/pods/frontend/.env.local` (mode 0640) |
| `PELICAN_URL` | `https://<fqdn>` |
| `PELICAN_API_KEY` | `<48-char Pelican application API token>` |
| `PELICAN_USER_ID` | `1` (the admin Pelican user that owns API operations) |
| `PELICAN_NODE_ID` | `1` (legacy single-node fallback) |
| `PELICAN_NODE_IDS` | `1,2` (load-distributed deploys) or `1` to pin to node 1 only |
| `PELICAN_NODE_TAILSCALE_IPS` | `2:100.92.124.106` — node id → tailnet IP map for `execInPod()` |
| `PODS_NODE_SSH_USER` | `podsadmin` (the user `execInPod` SSHes as for remote nodes) |
| `PELICAN_HERMES_EGG_ID` | `2` (egg ID after import) |
| `PELICAN_HERMES_IMAGE` | `pods-ml/sandbox-ubuntu:1.0` |
| `SESSION_SECRET` | `<64-char hex — cookie signer>` |
| `OAUTH_BASE_URL` | `https://app.pods.ml` (callbacks + cookie Domain derive from here) |
| `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` / `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET` | from Google Cloud Console |
| `GITHUB_CLIENT_ID` / `GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET` | from GitHub OAuth App |
| `RESEND` | Resend key for **auth + billing** emails (`hello@pods.ml`) |
| `RESEND_API_KEY` | Resend key for **agent** emails (`<slug>@inbox.bigcat.pw`) |
| `RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET` | Svix HMAC for inbound `email.received` |
| `AUTH_FROM_EMAIL` | `pods.ml <hello@pods.ml>` |
| `BILLING_FROM_EMAIL` | `pods.ml billing <billing@pods.ml>` |
| `BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_EMAIL` | seed admin user on first boot |
| `INTERNAL_RECONCILE_TOKEN` | secret for `/api/internal/*` cron endpoints |
| `INVOICE_KEY_ENCRYPTION_KEY` | AES key for invoice line-item encryption |
| `SOLANA_CLUSTER` / `SOLANA_RPC_URL` / `SOLANA_TREASURY_ADDRESS` | wallet sign-in / payments |
| `NODE_ENV` | `production` |
| `PODS_DOMAIN_ROOT` | `bigcat.pw` (defaults to this if unset) |
| `PODS_PUBLIC_HOST` | `app.pods.ml` (used in `EMAIL_OUTBOUND_PROXY` for new pods) |
| `EMAIL_DOMAIN` | `inbox.bigcat.pw` |
| `PODS_DB_PATH` | `/srv/pods/frontend/data/pods.db` |

## SQLite (FuelBorn user data)

| Key | Value |
|---|---|
| File | `/srv/pods/frontend/data/pods.db` (better-sqlite3 WAL) |
| Tables | `users`, `pod_metrics`, `pod_domains` |
| Backups | none yet — see roadmap |

## Other knobs

| Key | Value |
|---|---|
| `pods-ml-domain` sudo helper | `/usr/local/sbin/pods-ml-domain` (root:root 0755) |
| Sudoers grant | `/etc/sudoers.d/pods-ml-domain` (`podsadmin ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/pods-ml-domain`) |
| Caddy logs ACL | `setfacl g:podsadmin:r /var/log/caddy/pods/access.log` (so the frontend can tail) |
| `pelican_nw` docker network (node 1) | `172.18.0.0/16` (bridge driver) |
| `pelican_nw` docker network (node 2) | `172.21.0.0/16` (separate range for cross-node routing) |
| Node 1 → Node 2 SSH key | `/home/podsadmin/.ssh/id_ed25519` (used by `execInPod()` for remote pods) |

---

## Recovery checklist (if the VM dies)

1. `bash infra/azure-provision.sh` — re-create VM with same hostname.
2. `bash infra/bootstrap.sh` on the new VM — installs Docker, MariaDB, Pelican, Wings, Caddy.
3. **Restore from backup** (TODO — not yet implemented; pod data lives on `/srv/pods/`).
4. Reinstall `/etc/pelican/config.yml` and `/srv/pods/frontend/.env.local` from this file.
5. Reinstall `/etc/caddy/cloudflare.env` from this file.
6. Rebuild Caddy if needed (xcaddy + `caddy-dns/cloudflare` plugin — see `infra/INFRA.md`).
7. `php artisan p:user:make` to recreate the admin (or restore the SQL dump).
